{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "metadata": {
    "id": "pw8-somnus-drift",
    "name": "SOMNUS DRIFT",
    "author": "Patchwork Eight Engineering",
    "description": "A huge, deep, unhurried sleep pad -- the primary voice of the 'Sleep Jam' ambient piece. HUGE via two extra sub layers most patches don't bother with (sine an octave down at 0.65 AND sine two octaves down at 0.35, felt as much as heard) under a soft triangle-detuned core (ratios 0.996/1.0/1.004, triangle rather than saw so the detune beats read as gentle width, not edge). WARM via a dark-ish, low-resonance filter (1400Hz, res 0.1) and a Reverb pushed further than any prior preset (decay 11s, size 2.9, high-ratio 0.55 so the tail leans warm/dark rather than sparkly, low-ratio 1.7 so the sub content itself keeps ringing). SLOW/RESTFUL by design: a 6-second attack (nothing ever starts abruptly), an 8-second release, and the only modulation route is a very slow LFO1 -> Filter Cutoff breathe (0.035Hz, ~28s per cycle, matching a relaxed breathing pace, amount a gentle 6 semitones) -- deliberately no velocity routing or fast movement of any kind, since the goal is a sound with nothing for the ear to track. Designed to be layered with Aurora Pad (content/presets/aurora-pad.pw8) for the full 'Sleep Jam' piece -- Aurora's glassy shimmer sits on top of Somnus's depth without either patch needing to compromise.",
    "category": "pad",
    "moods": [
      "huge",
      "warm",
      "restful",
      "deep",
      "sleep"
    ],
    "genres": [
      "ambient",
      "sleep",
      "drone"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "pad",
      "sub-bass",
      "reverb-showcase",
      "sleep-jam"
    ],
    "createdAt": "2026-08-10T00:00:00Z",
